  "decision_summary": "Predicted high (F >= 20%) with moderate confidence. L4 verapamil absorption and permeability records (Fa 95-100%, high Caco-2 and MDR-MDCK Papp) show the absorption component is favorable for the verapamil-like chain shared by the query, so low verapamil F is first-pass-limited rather than absorption-limited. The most transferable direct F anchor, verapamil fasted 22% (17-29%), remains above threshold; gallopamil 15-23% and rabbit ketotifen 8% weaken but do not overturn the prediction. Confidence stays moderate because no direct F measurement exists for the exact query and the benzazepinone lactam first-pass behavior is unknown."
